# Personal architecture scratch notes — thinking in progress, not a spec.
/NOTES_ARCHITECTURE_SCRATCH.md
/POUCH_APP/DEVICE_SCREEN_DESIGN.md
/POUCH_APP/SCREENS_DESIGN.md

# NOTE: FOLLI_CONSOLE/assets/buttons/ is a synced mirror of SHARED_ASSETS/buttons/
# (Metro cannot reference assets above the Expo project root — see
# SHARED_ASSETS/README.md). It is deliberately COMMITTED rather than ignored,
# because CLAUDE.md documents `npx expo start --web` / `npx expo run:android`, which
# bypass the npm pre* hooks that would otherwise generate it. A fresh clone must work
# without running the sync first.
#     Edit the originals in SHARED_ASSETS/buttons/ — never the mirror.
#     `node SHARED_ASSETS/sync.mjs --check` fails if the two have drifted.

# Build artefacts and local state — never commit these.
node_modules/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
POUCH_APP/backend/folli.db
POUCH_APP/backend/folli.db-*
POUCH_APP/backend/server.log
POUCH_APP/frontend/vite.log
POUCH_APP/frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
# Vite's dependency pre-bundle cache, rewritten on every dev-server start.
POUCH_APP/frontend/.vite/

# Regenerated on every `python POUCH_APP/tools/visual_diff.py` run: the captured
# screenshots, the mockup crops they are compared against, and the diff maps.
# Several MB per run and meaningless outside the run that produced them — the
# committed record of how the screens look is VISUAL_REFERENCE/, not this.
POUCH_APP/tools/diff_output/
